Experiment 1: Complex Number Operations (Operator Overloading)
Start the program.
Create a class Complex with private data members real and imag.
Define a default constructor that sets the number to 0+0i, and a parameterized constructor that sets the given values.
Overload + as a member function. Create a temporary object where temp.real = real + c.real and temp.imag = imag + c.imag, then return it.
Overload * as a member function. Compute temp.real = real*c.real - imag*c.imag and temp.imag = real*c.imag + imag*c.real, then return it.
Overload >> as a friend function to read the real and imaginary parts from the user.
Overload << as a friend function to print the number in a+bi form. Print the + sign only when imag >= 0.
In main(), read c1 and c2, compute sum = c1 + c2 and product = c1 * c2, and display all four numbers.
Stop.





Experiment 2: Staff Payroll Management & Sorting
Start the program.
Create a class staff with data members Staff_ID, name, Basic_Salary, DA, HRA, Itax and NetSalary.
accept() reads the ID, name and basic salary.
calculate() computes:
DA = 25% of Basic
HRA = 800
Itax = 15% of Basic
NetSalary = Basic + DA + HRA − Itax
display() prints the pay slip, and getName() returns the name.
In main(), read n and create an array of n staff objects.
For each staff member, call accept() and then calculate().
Sort the array by name. For i = 0..n-2 and j = i+1..n-1, if s[i].getName() > s[j].getName(), swap s[i] and s[j].
Display the pay slip of every staff member in sorted order.
Stop.




Experiment 3: Publication Management & Exception Handling
