Experiment 7: Types of Inheritance
Start the program. Put each inheritance example in its own namespace so class names like Student and Result do not clash.
Single: Result derives from Student. A Result object calls both getStudent() and displayResult().
Multiple: Student derives from both Academic and Sports. It uses academicMarks(), sportsMarks() and its own display().
Multilevel: Person → Student → Result. A Result object can call the functions of all three classes.
Hierarchical: Developer and Manager both derive from Employee. Each object calls the common function and its own function.
Each namespace has a run() function that creates the objects and calls the functions.
main() calls the four run() functions in order.
Stop.



