Experiment 10: ATM Machine Simulation & Exception Handling
Start the program. Create custom exceptions ArithmeticException (derived from runtime_error) and IllegalArgumentException (derived from invalid_argument).
Create a class ATM with balance (initially Rs. 10000) and the functions checkBalance(), deposit() and withdraw().
deposit(): if amount <= 0, throw IllegalArgumentException. Otherwise add the amount to the balance.
withdraw():
If amount <= 0, throw IllegalArgumentException.
If amount > balance, throw ArithmeticException("Insufficient funds").
Otherwise subtract the amount from the balance.
In main(), run an infinite menu loop with the options 1. Balance, 2. Deposit, 3. Withdraw, 4. Exit.
Inside try, read the choice. If cin.fail(), clear the error, discard the bad input and throw IllegalArgumentException.
Use a switch to run the selected operation. Invalid choices throw IllegalArgumentException. Choice 4 prints a thank-you message and returns.
The catch blocks print the error message using e.what().
After each transaction, print “Transaction completed” (this acts like finally), then repeat the loop.
Stop.